scene: Nine years ago she was {Ns} second client; since then she has outlived her husband, two cats and four agencies. Now her legs have gone, her daughter has found a place in a care home, and on the last morning she asks {N} to help her choose what to take.
scene W: The care plan ends on Friday; the home will have its own. {N} wants the handover done right, so nothing she needs is lost between the two.
scene U: Nine years of mornings: {N} knows how she takes her tea, which pills make her sick, what she says when she is frightened. None of it is in the home's forms.
scene B: She has said more than once that {N} should have the gold watch on the dresser. The agency rules forbid gifts, and nobody else is in the room.
scene R: {N} has buried feelings about a dozen clients in nine years. This one is going to be hard, and {N} can feel it rising already.
scene G: People grow old, the legs go, the house is sold. {N} has seen it many times, and still it comes like the end of a season.
- W | do the handover by the book, and sign off nine years of care plans | v: conformity, benevolence | chance: 85
- U | write the home's staff a list of every small thing she likes | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | chance: 85
- B | take the watch she presses on you, and say nothing to the agency | v: power, hedonism | act: take the watch she presses on them, and say nothing to the agency | mark: hid a wrong | closed: approval: gifts from clients are forbidden; backfire: the daughter asks where the watch went, and a disciplinary follows | chance: 75
- R | hand in your notice that week: nine years of goodbyes is enough | v: self-direction | drops: care worker | chance: 85
- G | help her choose the few things that matter, and let the rest go | v: benevolence, tradition (acceptance) | chance: 78
- W>U | sign up for the end-of-life care course the agency runs | v: achievement, benevolence | grants: home nursing | chance: 80
- U>B | ask for the coordinator's job, off the road, now that you know every round | v: achievement, power | title: shift manager | chance: 55
- B>R | slip the home's manager some chocolates, to get her the garden-view room | v: benevolence, hedonism | chance: 60
- R>G | cry with her over the boxes, and let it be what it is | v: benevolence | chance: 85
- G>W | ask the home to let her bring the cat, and offer to visit them both | v: benevolence | chance: 40
works: She goes in her best coat, with the photographs and a small bag of what matters, and holds {Ns} hand at the door.
works: Two weeks later a card arrives at the agency in a shaky hand, with {Ns} name on it.
fails: She cries all the way to the home, and {N} cannot shake it for a week.
fails: The handover is lost in the home's paperwork, and the first news from her daughter is bad.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- soldier, new (tenure 0-1): calls RG (cycle s3)

== week six of basic training
tier: everyday
at: army
stages: juvenile young_adult adult
age: 16-30
calls: RG
holds: soldier
tenure: 0-1
rate: 2
once: yes
tone: mixed
life: work, body
horizon: week
roles: boss, colleague, parent, the other recruits
earth: halfway through basic training: the runs before dawn, the kit inspections, and a section that sinks or swims together
times: Every new soldier, once, at 16 to 30, halfway through basic training; it lasts about 10 weeks in the US Army and 14 in the British Army
scene: Week six of basic training: up at five, three miles before breakfast, kit laid out to the inch for inspection, and a corporal who finds something wrong every time. One recruit in {Ns} section is falling behind, and the whole section pays for it.
scene W: Everything here has a right way: the bed, the boots, the drill, the way to stand. {N} finds an odd comfort in it.
scene U: {N} has worked out what the corporal checks first, and in what order. There is a system under all the shouting.
scene B: The best recruit leads the section at the passing-out parade. {N} wants it, and watches who else does.
scene R: {Ns} feet are blistered and {Ns} lungs burn on every hill, and still, at the top, {N} feels more alive than ever before.
scene G: Six weeks ago they were twelve strangers; now they eat, sleep, run and suffer together. {N} has never been part of anything like it.
- W | report every slip the struggling recruit makes, so the section stops paying | v: conformity | mark: made an enemy | closed: approval: informing on a comrade; backfire: the section freezes them out | chance: 75
- U | learn the drill and the kit list cold, until you can do them in the dark | v: achievement | mark: learned a skill | chance: 80
- B | push to lead the section at the parade, and make sure the corporal sees it | v: power, achievement | chance: 60
- R | run the hills on the blisters, and finish every run near the front | habit | body: heavy | v: stimulation, achievement | grants: keeping fit | self_control: + | chance: 80
- G | lean on the section like family, and let them lean on you | v: benevolence (in-group) | act: lean on the section like family, and let them lean back | mark: made a friend | chance: 80
- W>R | carry the struggling recruit's pack up the last hill as well as your own | body: heavy | v: benevolence | mark: helped someone in need | closed: approval: against the instructors' orders; backfire: both recruits punished | chance: 65
- U>G | set up a buddy system so nobody in the section falls behind | v: benevolence, security | chance: 75
- B>W | make yourself the corporal's favourite with every extra duty going | v: power, achievement | chance: 75
- R>U | volunteer for the hardest test on the course, to find out what you are made of | body: heavy | v: stimulation, achievement | chance: 60
- G>B | go home: sign the discharge papers while you still can | v: security | drops: soldier | mark: came home | self_control: - | chance: 85
works: At the passing-out parade {N} marches in step, and somewhere in the crowd {parent} is crying.
works: {N} comes through week six fitter and steadier than ever, and the corporal, once, nods.
fails: A shin injury puts {N} back three weeks, to start again with a new section.
fails: The section is punished for {Ns} mistake, and the barrack room goes cold for days.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- soldier, settled (tenure 2-7): calls UB (cycle s4)

== the papers to sign on again
tier: everyday
at: army
stages: young_adult adult
age: 18-40
calls: UB
holds: soldier
tenure: 2-7
rate: 1
once: yes
tone: mixed
life: work, home
horizon: years
roles: colleague, parent, partner, friend
earth: your first term of service is nearly up: sign on for more, retrain, go on a tour abroad, or leave
times: Most soldiers, once, at the end of a first term; a first term is often four years or more in the US and British armies (estimate)
scene: {Ns} first term is up in the spring, and the papers to sign on for six more years are in the drawer. {colleague} is going on a tour abroad in the summer and wants {N} along; a private firm has offered twice the pay; and the people at home want {N} back.
scene W: {N} took an oath, and the unit is short of hands. The army made {N}; signing again feels like the honourable thing.
scene U: The army will retrain anyone who signs on: medic, signals, engineer, a trade for life. {N} has read every leaflet twice.
scene B: Six more years means the stripe, the pension and a trade paid for. The private firm means money now. {N} lays the numbers side by side.
scene R: A tour means somewhere new, real work, the people who matter most at {Ns} side. A desk means none of that.
scene G: {N} has missed three birthdays and a funeral at home. The town, the family and the old friends feel further away with every leave.
- W | sign on for six more years, and keep the oath you took | binds | identity | v: conformity, tradition | mark: kept your word | chance: 85
- U | sign on, but only to retrain as a combat medic | binds | v: achievement, benevolence | grants: emergency care | chance: 70
- B | leave for the private security firm abroad, at twice the pay | binds | identity | v: achievement, power | drops: soldier | title: veteran | death_if_fails: 0.002 | mark: moved away | chance: 65
- R | put in for special forces selection, the hardest course there is | body: heavy | v: stimulation, achievement | self_control: + | chance: 15
- G | go where the platoon goes on the summer tour, as the others do | v: benevolence (in-group), tradition | death_if_fails: 0.001 | chance: 70
- W>G | leave at the end of the term and go home to the family, as promised | v: tradition, benevolence | drops: soldier | title: veteran | mark: came home | chance: 85
- U>W | sign on with the engineers, and learn a trade the army pays for | v: security, achievement | chance: 70
- B>U | get the army to pay for every licence and course going, for later | v: achievement, security | grants: lorry or bus licence | chance: 80
- R>B | sign on the same day for the bonus, and spend it on a car | binds | v: hedonism, power | grants: car | self_control: - | chance: 88
- G>R | take a month's leave first, and walk the hills at home before deciding | v: self-direction, hedonism | chance: 75
works: {N} signs, or does not, with a clear head, and the spring comes in on a new footing.
works: The choice opens doors {N} did not know were there, and the first months prove it right.
fails: The choice goes wrong in the first months, and {N} wonders, on bad nights, about the other road.
fails: The paperwork drags on for months, and {N} spends the summer stuck between two lives.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- soldier, senior (tenure 8-60): calls WR (cycle s4)

== a section of nineteen-year-olds
tier: everyday
at: army
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 24-55
calls: WR
holds: soldier
tenure: 8-60
rate: .5
once: yes
tone: mixed
life: work, community
horizon: months
roles: colleague, boss, the young soldiers, partner
earth: after many years in the army you lead a section of soldiers barely out of school, on what may be your last tour abroad
times: Some long-serving soldiers, once, as junior leaders after eight years or more; most soldiers leave before ten years (estimate)
scene: {N} has more years in the army than any of the section has been out of school. They are on a tour abroad in a hot, dusty camp, one of the corporals is too hard on the youngest, and every morning eight young soldiers look at {N} to know what the day holds.
scene W: {N} answers for all eight of them: their kit, their discipline and, above all, their getting home. {N} does not take it lightly.
scene U: There are a hundred things {N} learned the hard way that are in no manual. The young ones learn them slowly, or not at all.
scene B: The staff job at headquarters is open: a desk, a rank, a pension that climbs, and no more patrols. {N} has been asked to apply.
scene R: {N} still loves it: the early starts, the heat, the jokes, the trust. And knows the body will not take many more years of it.
scene G: The youngest of the section reminds {N} of {Ns} own first year, down to the way he laces his boots. {N} feels like the old hand in a family.
- W | take the lead on every patrol yourself, so the youngest do not have to | body: heavy | v: benevolence, security | death_if_fails: 0.003 | chance: 70
- U | teach them every evening the things no manual says | habit | v: benevolence | grants: teaching | chance: 85
- B | apply for the staff job at headquarters, and the rank that goes with it | v: power, security | grants: rank | chance: 60
- R | sign on for one more tour, because nothing else feels like this | binds | v: stimulation, hedonism | chance: 85
- G | write to each of their families, the way your old sergeant did | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 85
- W>G | report the corporal who is too hard on the youngest, through the proper channels | v: universalism, benevolence | mark: made an enemy | chance: 60
- U>W | take them out on the route you worked out, not the one ordered | v: security, self-direction | closed: approval: departing from a patrol order; backfire: a charge, and the stripe taken | death_if_fails: 0.003 | chance: 60
- B>U | use your contacts to put the brightest of them on the officers' course | v: benevolence, achievement | chance: 60
- R>B | take the corporal aside, and make him afraid to pick on the youngest again | v: power | closed: law: threatening a fellow soldier; backfire: a charge, and the stripe taken | chance: 70
- G>R | hand in your notice for the end of the tour, and go and live | v: self-direction, hedonism | drops: soldier | title: veteran | chance: 75
works: All eight of them come home at the end of the tour, and the youngest shakes {Ns} hand at the airport.
works: The section pulls together under {N}, and {boss} says so in the report.
fails: The tour goes hard, and {N} brings home a weight that does not lift for a long time.
fails: The choice costs {N} the stripe, the trust of the young ones, or both.

# ---------------------------------------------------------------- teacher, new (tenure 0-1): calls WR (cycle s2)

== the back row on the first Monday
tier: everyday
at: school
stages: young_adult adult mature
age: 21-70
calls: WR
holds: teacher
tenure: 0-1
rate: 2
once: yes
tone: mixed
life: work, school
horizon: moment
roles: colleague, boss, the pupils, mentor
earth: your first class of your own on a Monday in September: thirty fourteen-year-olds, and a back row already testing you
times: Every new teacher, once, in the first week of the first term; nearly 1 in 3 new teachers in England leave within five years (DfE workforce statistics)
scene: Monday, September, room 14: {Ns} first class of {Ns} own. Thirty fourteen-year-olds, a lesson plan typed at midnight, and a back row that has already started, very quietly, to test the new teacher.
scene W: The seating plan is printed, the rules are on the wall, and the training said the first five minutes decide the year. {N} intends to make them count.
scene U: The lesson plan is timed to the minute, with three activities and a summing-up. {N} also has a hunch it will not survive the first ten minutes.
scene B: The back row has a leader, a tall boy with a quick tongue whom the others watch before they laugh. {N} sees that the class turns on him.
scene R: {Ns} heart is going like a drum. Somewhere under the fear is the thing that made {N} want to teach in the first place: the moment a room lights up.
scene G: These are other people's children, each with a home, a story and a bad night behind them. {N} looks at thirty faces and wonders who they are.
- W | set the seating plan and the rules in the first five minutes, and keep them | habit | v: conformity, security | self_control: + | chance: 70
- U | follow the timed plan, and note what works and what does not for next time | v: achievement, self-direction | chance: 75
- B | win over the boy the back row follows, and the rest will come | v: power | chance: 65
- R | put the plan aside and open with the most surprising thing you know | v: stimulation | chance: 60
- G | learn every name by Friday, and ask each of them one thing about themselves | v: benevolence | self_control: + | chance: 75
- W>B | keep the whole back row in at break, to show who is in charge | v: power, conformity | closed: approval: a whole-row detention on the first day; backfire: parents complain, and the head has words | chance: 60
- U>R | turn the lesson into a puzzle they solve in teams, against the clock | v: stimulation | chance: 65
- B>G | strike a deal with the back row: quiet now, their music at the end | v: security, hedonism | chance: 75
- R>W | raise your voice, once and hard, the first time the back row laughs | v: conformity, security | chance: 60
- G>U | ask the teacher next door, who has had them two years, what they are like | v: tradition, self-direction | chance: 80
works: By the bell the back row is laughing with {N}, not at {N}, and a quiet girl at the front stays behind to ask a question.
works: The lesson works better than it had any right to, and {N} sits in the empty room afterwards, grinning.
fails: The back row takes the lesson apart, and {N} drives home and sits in the car outside the house for twenty minutes.
fails: The head of department walks in at the worst moment, and writes something down.

