earth: a few years into teaching, the head of year post is advertised, the union wants a new rep, and a school abroad is hiring
times: Many teachers who stay, once, a few years in; most schools fill middle posts from their own staff (estimate)
scene: Four years in, {N} knows the school, the corridors and which photocopier jams. The head of year post is on the staffroom board, the union wants a new rep, and a school abroad is advertising for someone in {Ns} subject.
scene W: A head of year answers for two hundred pupils: their behaviour, their attendance, the calls home. {N} believes someone has to do it properly.
scene U: {N} has started to wonder how pupils really learn, and whether the school teaches the best way. There is a master's course on Tuesday evenings.
scene B: The post comes with a pay point, a seat at the leadership meetings and a first step toward running a school. {N} sees where the ladder goes.
scene R: A school by the sea, in another country, in another language. {N} reads the advert three times and cannot stop thinking about it.
scene G: {Ns} first class is now in its final year. {N} would like to see them through to the end.
